<?xml version="1.0"?>
<?xml-stylesheet type="text/xsl" href="http://jsbsim.sf.net/JSBSimScript.xsl"?>
<runscript
       name="Mi-17 hover at 100 ft AGL, hold 15 minutes"
       xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://jsbsim.sf.net/JSBSimScript.xsd">

  <description>
    Climbs from a ground start to a 100 ft AGL hover and holds it for
    15 minutes (900s). Built directly on scripts/test_mi17_hover.xml's
    validated settle/bias-ramp/collective-ramp/handoff sequence (see
    that script's own description and this branch's commit history for
    the two real bugs found and fixed there: a handoff-timing gate that
    let the aircraft rocket to 1197 ft AGL before altitude hold ever
    engaged, and a collective-ramp race that silently undid the post-
    handoff trim). Only two things differ from that script:

    1. Initial conditions are "ground running steady state", not a
       cold/instant start: the aircraft begins on the ground
       (initialize="reset00", engines off) and holds flat collective
       for a full 120s -- the window scripts/test_mi17_ground_run_idle.
       xml measured the RPM governor actually needing to converge to
       the real 192 RPM target (shaft-rpm ~187 at 30s, ~191.6 at 60s,
       192.0 by 90-120s), not an arbitrary guess. JSBSim's initialize
       IC files only support marking an engine running at t=0, not
       injecting an already-converged shaft-rpm/governor-integrator
       state directly (checked src/initialization/FGInitialCondition.
       cpp -- no arbitrary property-override support there), so
       "ground running steady state" is reached by actually running
       the settle window, not skipped via some IC shortcut. Only once
       that's genuinely reached does the climb begin, exactly as in
       test_mi17_hover.xml.

    2. ap/altitude-target-ft is field elevation (2283.5, reset00.xml)
       + 100 = 2383.5, not +30. The closed-loop climb-out (ramp
       collective straight to hover trim, ~0.092, while engaging
       altitude hold at the same instant) and the afcs.xml altitude-
       hold gains (P=0.005, rate=-0.05, ki=0.0000002) are unchanged
       from the validated hover script -- this is the same aircraft and
       the same closed loop, just a different target altitude. See
       test_mi17_hover.xml's description for the full derivation of the
       trim value and the sign-bug fix behind the rate gain.

    Holding "for 15 minutes" needs a start-of-hold reference point, but
    JSBSim scripts cannot declare their own property elements (a set or
    condition element referencing an undeclared property throws at
    runtime -- confirmed the hard way against src/math/FGPropertyValue.
    cpp), so there is no clean way to dynamically latch "the moment the
    aircraft first settles near 100 ft" into a property and compute a
    15-minutes-later deadline from it within this script alone. Instead
    the hold window is anchored on real data: scripts/test_mi17_hover.
    xml's long run (target 30 ft AGL, same aircraft/gains) crossed
    h-agl-ft=100 around t=1500-1700s with v-down-fps already under
    0.12 fps there, i.e. already close to settled. This script's
    hold window is set generously later than that, t=2000-2900s (an
    exact 900s span), to give real margin for this run's own dynamics
    (different target altitude, so not an identical trajectory) to
    actually settle before the window starts. This is an ESTIMATE, not
    a guarantee -- the CSV output below is the authoritative record;
    check it after running to confirm the aircraft was genuinely within
    a tight band of 100 ft AGL for that whole window, and re-anchor the
    checkpoint times if it wasn't.
  </description>

  <use aircraft="mi17" initialize="reset00"/>

  <!-- CSV trace of the full run, 1 Hz; the authoritative record for
       verifying the hold window actually covers a genuine, settled
       100 ft AGL hover; see the description above. Script-scoped, not
       added to aircraft/mi17/mi17.xml (JSBSim scripts support their
       own <output>, loaded via FGScript::LoadScript() ->
       FDMExec->GetOutput()->Load()), so it only applies to this run. -->
  <output name="mi17_hover_100ft_15min.csv" type="CSV" rate="1">
    <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
    <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
    <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
    <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
    <property> fcs/collective-cmd-norm </property>
    <property> ap/altitude-hold-on </property>
    <property> ap/altitude-integral-cmd </property>
    <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
  </output>

  <run start="0.0" end="2960.0" dt="0.0075">

    <event name="start" persistent="false">
      <!-- Real, governor-moderated start via FGTurboshaft's starter-cmd/
           cutoff-cmd, not propulsion/set-running; see scripts/test_mi17_
           ground_run_idle.xml's identical event comment for the full
           derivation, including why this needs ge 0.1 rather than
           ge 0.0. Engine 2 (tail rotor, FGElectric) keeps its own simple
           per-engine set-running. -->
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 0.1 </condition>
      <set name="propulsion/engine[0]/starter-cmd" value="1"/>
      <set name="propulsion/engine[1]/starter-cmd" value="1"/>
      <set name="propulsion/engine[0]/cutoff-cmd" value="0"/>
      <set name="propulsion/engine[1]/cutoff-cmd" value="0"/>
      <set name="propulsion/engine[2]/set-running" value="1"/>
      <set name="fcs/collective-cmd-norm" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="fcs/adj/collective-bias" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="ap/attitude-hold-on" value="1.0"/>
    </event>

    <event name="hold-attitude" persistent="true">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 0.0 </condition>
      <set name="ap/attitude-hold-on" value="1.0"/>
    </event>

    <event name="hold-ground-settle" persistent="true">
      <!-- Ground running steady state: 120s, measured (not guessed) in
           scripts/test_mi17_ground_run_idle.xml. -->
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec le 119.999 </condition>
      <set name="fcs/collective-cmd-norm" value="0.0"/>
      <set name="fcs/adj/collective-bias" value="0.0"/>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint ground-steady-state (110s)" persistent="false">
      <!-- Confirms steady state was actually reached before the climb
           begins, not just assumed. -->
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 110.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
        <property> fcs/throttle-cmd-norm[0] </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="ramp-collective-bias" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 120.0 </condition>
      <set name="fcs/adj/collective-bias" value="0.15" action="FG_RAMP" tc="20.0"/>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/n1 </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="hold trim collective, engage altitude hold" persistent="true" continuous="true">
      <!-- Closed-loop climb-out: replaces the old open-loop ramp to
           0.75 followed by a late handoff/backoff to 0.68. Ramps
           collective directly to the true hover-trim value (~0.092)
           and engages altitude hold at the same instant, t=140 (once
           the bias ramp above is done). See test_mi17_hover.xml's
           description and this event's identical one there for the
           full derivation of the trim value and why continuous="true"
           (not just persistent="true") is required for the ramp's
           <set> to remain the permanent owner of fcs/collective-cmd-
           norm for the rest of the run. No h-agl-ft gate is needed:
           the collective baseline here is already genuine trim, not an
           aggressive climb target, so there is no large open-loop
           excursion for a late gate to guard against. -->
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 140.0 </condition>
      <set name="ap/altitude-target-ft" value="2383.5"/>
      <set name="ap/altitude-hold-on" value="1.0"/>
      <set name="fcs/collective-cmd-norm" value="0.092" action="FG_RAMP" tc="10.0"/>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> fcs/collective-cmd-norm </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint 165s" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 165.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> fcs/collective-cmd-norm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/collective-ctrl-rad </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/thrust-lbs </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint 185s" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 185.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> fcs/collective-cmd-norm </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint 30s post-handoff" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 245.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> fcs/collective-cmd-norm </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint 500s" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 500.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> ap/altitude-integral-cmd </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint 1000s" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 1000.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> ap/altitude-integral-cmd </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="checkpoint 1500s" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 1500.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> ap/altitude-integral-cmd </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <!-- Hold window: t=2000-2900s (an exact 900s span), anchored on
         the previous run's convergence timing; see the description
         above for why this is an estimate, and check the CSV output
         to confirm h-agl-ft actually stayed close to 100 for this
         whole span before treating this run as a validated 15-minute
         hold. -->
    <event name="hold window start (2000s)" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 2000.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> ap/altitude-integral-cmd </property>
        <property> fcs/collective-cmd-norm </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="hold window +3min (2180s)" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 2180.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="hold window +6min (2360s)" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 2360.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="hold window +9min (2540s)" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 2540.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="hold window +12min (2720s)" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 2720.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

    <event name="hold window complete, +15min (2900s)" persistent="false">
      <condition> simulation/sim-time-sec ge 2900.0 </condition>
      <notify>
        <property> simulation/sim-time-sec </property>
        <property> position/h-agl-ft </property>
        <property> velocities/v-down-fps </property>
        <property> velocities/vt-fps </property>
        <property> attitude/pitch-rad </property>
        <property> attitude/roll-rad </property>
        <property> velocities/r-rad_sec </property>
        <property> ap/altitude-integral-cmd </property>
        <property> propulsion/gearbox[0]/shaft-rpm </property>
        <property> propulsion/engine[0]/thrust-lbs </property>
      </notify>
    </event>

  </run>

</runscript>
